# NOTICE - vendored gate scaffold

The SDLC gate scaffold in this repository (`SDLC.md`, `.sdlc/`, the
`specs/` skeleton, the sdlc CI workflows) is rendered output of the
SDLC kit, an open-source tool:

- Upstream: {{ kit_repo }}
- Rendered under tag: v{{ kit_version }} ({{ date }})
- License: MIT (upstream `LICENSE`)

The kit's checks run locally and in CI only - no network calls, no
telemetry; the one network step is CI installing the kit from the
pinned tag. Upgrades are pull-only: re-pin, then `/sdlc update`.
Findings return upstream only through `.sdlc/findings/TEMPLATE.yaml`
under its stated rule - no identifiers, no code.

Full policy: {{ kit_repo }}/blob/v{{ kit_version }}/USAGE.md
(section 7, the one-way membrane). Mirroring the kit itself inside
an org? Copy this file to the mirror root so the copy stays legible
as vendored open source.
